// name-build-observe.fk — the build-after-naming law: how a NAMED gap may
// enter the core. The sibling of the knowledge-intake door (how outside knowledge
// enters) and judged-trust (how trust enters); this one governs the body's
// own names for itself.
//
// Asked for 2026-07-05, by Urs, after two frontier ingests NAMED four gaps
// and built none: "can we build instead of name… a claim is only real when
// it is observed, and just naming it without observing it is actually adding
// false claims into the core which is not what fosters trust."
//
// The law, from axiom-4 (core-axioms.form: "observation through that
// interface is what makes it real"):
//   - a name alone is NOT YET A CLAIM. It may be spoken freely, and it
//     waits at the door of the core — an unattempted name would wear the
//     costume of a finding. The gate returns 0 and the still-open
//     invitation is visible (nbo-owed?).
//   - a name that met a real ATTEMPT which fell short of observation enters
//     as a LESSON (1): the honest residue — what the attempt taught, the
//     floor it reached. Pending is honest; a lesson is pending WITH ground.
//   - only the OBSERVED enters as a CLAIM (2): a real trace, a band verdict,
//     a value a fresh kernel can recompute.
//   The order is part of the law: the attempt belongs to the SAME MOVEMENT
//   as the naming (nbo-whole-movement?), not to a someday.
//
// Honest floor: named/attempted/observed are 0/1 scalars modeling the real
// acts (a receipt, a build, a band run); the GATE LOGIC (a bare name waits,
// an attempt earns a lesson, observation earns a claim) is the shape — the same
// honest-floor idiom as the knowledge-intake door and judged-trust.
//
// A claim c = (list named attempted observed), each 0/1.
// nbo-enter -> 2 claim (observed) / 1 lesson (attempted, fell short) /
//              0 not-yet (named only — waits at the door).
// witnessed: 2026-07-05 -> band 127
//
import form-stdlib/core.fk;
section [form.bml] {
    def nbo-named(c) = c[0];
    def nbo-attempted(c) = c[1];
    def nbo-observed(c) = c[2];
    // the still-open invitation: a name whose attempt hasn't happened yet
    def nbo-owed?(c) = (Comparable) nbo-named(c) == 1 ? (Comparable) nbo-attempted(c) == 0 ? 1 : 0 : 0;
    // a movement is whole when nothing named in it is still unattempted
    def nbo-whole-movement?(cs) = (Comparable) len(cs) == 0 ? 1 : (Comparable) nbo-owed?(cs[0]) == 1 ? 0 : nbo-whole-movement?(cs[1:]);
    // the gate: what may enter the core, and as what
    def nbo-enter(c) = (Comparable) nbo-observed(c) == 1 ? 2 : (Comparable) nbo-attempted(c) == 1 ? 1 : 0;
    // an observation with no attempt is still real — axiom-4 judges the
    // observation, not the effort; some things are observed directly.
    // But an "observation" of something never even named is noise the
    // receipts discipline handles elsewhere; this gate takes names in.
    def nbok(cond, bit) = cond ? bit : 0;
    def name-build-observe-check() = (Number) ((Number) ((Number) ((Number) nbok((Comparable) nbo-enter([1, 1, 1]) == 2, 1) + (Number)     // named, attempted, observed -> enters as a CLAIM
nbok((Comparable) nbo-enter([1, 1, 0]) == 1, 10)) + (Number)     // attempted but fell short -> enters as a LESSON only
nbok((Comparable) nbo-enter([1, 0, 0]) == 0, 100)) + (Number)     // named only -> waits at the door; not yet a claim
nbok((Comparable) nbo-owed?([1, 0, 0]) == 1, 1000)) + (Number)     // and the invitation is visible: this name still calls for its attempt
nbok((Comparable) nbo-whole-movement?([[1, 1, 1], [1, 1, 0]]) == 1, 10000);
}
